# Frontend Architecture Rules

Use Next.js App Router with TypeScript strict mode.

Folder structure:
- app/(auth)
- app/(super-admin)
- app/(tenant)
- components/ui
- components/layout
- features
- hooks
- lib
- store
- types
- constants

Use:
- React Hook Form for forms
- Zod for validation
- TanStack Query for server state
- Zustand only for lightweight client state
- shadcn/ui for UI components
- Tailwind CSS for styling

Do not put all logic inside pages.
Move reusable logic into:
- hooks
- lib
- features
- components

Every page should handle:
- loading state
- error state
- empty state
- permission state where needed

Do not store secrets in NEXT_PUBLIC variables.
Never rely only on frontend permission checks. Backend must enforce permissions.

## Responsive UI Rules

All UI must be fully responsive for:
- desktop
- laptop
- tablet
- mobile

Use mobile-first responsive design.

Every page, layout, table, form, modal, sidebar, header, and dashboard card must work properly on small and large screens.

Responsive requirements:
- sidebar should collapse into mobile drawer
- tables should support horizontal scroll or mobile-friendly card layout
- forms should stack on mobile
- modals should fit mobile screens
- buttons should not overflow
- dashboards should use responsive grid
- text should remain readable on all screen sizes
- spacing should adjust for mobile and tablet
- avoid fixed widths unless necessary
- use Tailwind responsive classes like sm:, md:, lg:, xl:, 2xl:

Before finishing any frontend task, check responsive behavior for mobile, tablet, and desktop.